10417.docs:
Checked `Timespec` addition. Returns `None` if overflow occurred.

# Panics

If `0 <= .tv_nsec < 1_000_000_000` doesn't hold, this function may
panic or return unexpected results.

# Example

```
use rustix::event::Timespec;

assert_eq!(
    Timespec {
        tv_sec: 1,
        tv_nsec: 2
    }
    .checked_add(Timespec {
        tv_sec: 30,
        tv_nsec: 40
    }),
    Some(Timespec {
        tv_sec: 31,
        tv_nsec: 42
    })
);
assert_eq!(
    Timespec {
        tv_sec: 0,
        tv_nsec: 999_999_999
    }
    .checked_add(Timespec {
        tv_sec: 0,
        tv_nsec: 2
    }),
    Some(Timespec {
        tv_sec: 1,
        tv_nsec: 1
    })
);
assert_eq!(
    Timespec {
        tv_sec: i64::MAX,
        tv_nsec: 999_999_999
    }
    .checked_add(Timespec {
        tv_sec: 0,
        tv_nsec: 1
    }),
    None
);
```

